tandard BSSA convention. Now I need to organize these sources into detailed chunk reviews, so I'll write them out methodically. I'm structuring the first chunk file with the seismic design criteria content—starting with the section header, then working through the regulatory references from ASCE 7-22 and IBC 2021, the MCER definition and scaling approach, the design spectrum formulas with the (2/3) factor, and the SMS and SM1 back-calculations, finishing with an audit note. I'm seeing that the formula continues with the SD1 definition and the conditional cases for T*, all within what appears to be two consecutive display math blocks separated only by `$$ $$`. I need to clarify whether Quarto treats this as a single block or two separate ones, since the spacing and delimiter pattern affects how the audit footnote should be placed. I'm ready to finalize the chunk files with properly formatted footnotes using ASCII characters only, keeping the original KB content unchanged while adding audit notes where needed.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4050,"cache_read_input_tokens":64096,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4050,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5655a3d-d1a5-49f5-9bdd-236b5edf4893","uuid":"3ad6e2b6-307a-4563-963a-3f4e8d261e02"}
